course: dictionary
lesson: 10139
title: The thrill of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thrill is a sudden, strong feeling of excitement and pleasure. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «You watch a snow leopard creep across a cliff for three thrilling minutes.» Watching a leopard creep along a cliff is exciting, so thrilling means very exciting.
explain: Thrill can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a thrill is the feeling itself: «Toad enjoyed the thrill of telling one after promising not to.» As a verb, to thrill someone is to make them very excited and happy. Thrilled, an adjective, means very pleased.
explain: Feelings like thrill can differ from person to person. «Many people enjoy being scared by a film because it is a thrill with no real danger, like a roller coaster; other people simply don't, and both are fine.» Nobody has to enjoy every thrill, and that is fine.
fact: A thrill is a sudden strong feeling of excitement and pleasure.
fact: To thrill someone means to make them very excited and happy.
fact: «Thrilled» means very pleased. «Thrilling» means very exciting.
fact: Phrases you may meet: the thrill of, a thrill ride, thrills and spills, thrill seeker.
fact: Near the spot, the Rat feels «a faint sort of electric thrill» through his arm, so a thrill can be small as well as big.
exercise: «You watch a snow leopard creep across a cliff for three thrilling minutes.» What does thrilling mean here? | Very boring | Very cold | Very dark | *Very exciting
exercise: Which word means very pleased? | Thrifty | Threw | Thrown | *Thrilled
exercise: «Toad enjoyed the thrill of telling one after promising not to.» In this sentence, what is a thrill? | A loud noise | A promise to keep a secret | A kind of cliff | *A sudden strong feeling of excitement and pleasure
test: «Near the spot the Rat feels a faint sort of electric thrill through his arm.» Is the Rat's thrill big or small? | Huge, like a storm | *Small, a faint feeling | Painful, like a cut | Not a feeling at all
test: What does «to thrill someone» mean? | To make them very sleepy | To tell them a secret | To hurt them badly | *To make them very excited and happy
exam: Why can a film be a thrill for one person and not for another? | Because films are always boring | Because only children enjoy thrills | Because films are always dangerous | *Because people feel excitement in different ways, and both feelings are fine
